# Docs commands

Reader-facing steps install once, then use `wsm`.

```sh
python3 -m pip install -e packages/python
export WSM_TEACHER_URL="https://example.invalid"
export WSM_TEACHER_MODEL="your-model-id"
export WSM_TEACHER_API_KEY="your-key"
wsm run "Improve signed addition. Inspect the weights and test your changes." \
  --task addition --output runs/addition
```

Do not write `.venv/bin/python`, `.venv/bin/wsm`, or `python3 -m venv`. Do not make a virtual environment the subject of a step.

The first task in `README.md`, the docs homepage, the quickstart, and `docs/wsm.md` is connecting a model and editing a weight. Set `WSM_TEACHER_URL`, `WSM_TEACHER_MODEL`, and `WSM_TEACHER_API_KEY`, then run `wsm run` with `--task addition`. The next example is one `inspect` and one `edit`. Do not open that path with a scripted offline demo.

`INTEGRATION_PYTHON` may be `$PWD/.venv/bin/python` in the verification notes. That script needs a filesystem path. That line is the only exception.
